<title>SINGAPORE: Philippines to import more pork and beef in 1997.</title>
<headline>Philippines to import more pork and beef in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines will increase the amount of frozen pork imports it will allow into the country in 1997 to as much as 53,000 tonnes against 1996 imports of 2,500 tonnes, Agriculture Secretary Salvador Escudero III said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Manila allowed imports this year of up to 49,900 tonnes of pork but Philippine livestock companies imported only about 2,500 tonnes, he told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>Beef imports should rise to 47,000 tonnes in 1997 from an estimated 42,000 tonnes this year.</p>
</text>
